From e6d857984408e61badbfd1693401027eb4f6fe0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:49:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] accel/ane: h17: take the cold-boot SoC layout from the
 platform

The staged backend hardcodes the T8140: ANE_SYS and the two child power
states at PMGR +0x290/+0xc000/+0xc008, the "apple,t8140-ane-dart" DART
compatible, four DAPF ranges, the 26.6.2 TEXT pin, and the start at boot.
Move these into struct ane_fw_platform so another SoC with the same H17
firmware interface can describe its own layout, and dispatch the staged
path on the platform's owner instead of on soc == 0x8140.

Add cold_unmeasured for a SoC whose cold-boot sequence has not been
measured yet. Such a platform needs no TEXT pin: with a loader hand-off
the observer is installed and binds without holding ANE_SYS, logs the
preload TEXT digest and the PMGR words, and accepts only the read-only
probe stage. Every acquiring stage refuses before any power, DMA or
engine access. A preload whose layout does not match the platform is
now logged with its addresses and sizes, and an apple,ane-type in the
DT must match the platform's.

The T8140 values are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
